sub:assertion {
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/morphoeval-delphi10000-dactylioceras-commune-turing-wavelength-s0> pk:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-dactylioceras-commune-turing-wavelength-s0-overall> .
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-dactylioceras-commune-turing-wavelength-s0-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
        rdfs:label "Dactylioceras commune Turing k_c at 24 µm (pass 2) — MorphoEval overall 89.5/100" ;
        dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
        dct:description "Pass 2 keeps lambda_c = 24.19 µm (2.419e-05 m) at 181 Ma. Numerical growth rates of the Schnakenberg PDE match analytical sigma(k) with Pearson r = 0.99991 and RMSE = 0.00095. Equal diffusion is stable at k_c (sigma = -0.431) while the ratio 7.2 is unstable (sigma = +0.0297). Scaling both diffusivities by 0.64, 1, 1.44, and 1.96 moves lambda_c through 19.35, 24.19, 29.03, and 33.87 µm. The Whitby photograph (57 mm, CC BY 2.0) has 44 outer ribs at 3.484 mm spacing, which holds 144 waves of 24.19 µm, more than the Ceratites organ-scale interval (45.0) and the Placenticeras organ-scale interval (104.6). The growth GIF is 12 frames at 640 px and ends on the specimen (CV similarity 96.0). D_f = 1.55 remains a catalogue value: the photo shows the ribbed exterior. Overall 89.5/100 (faithfulness 89.4, reproducibility 89.6); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit 8c95fb91d41c76d640c8216d24030d8fd3768487; environment: . Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 92, Morphological realism / specimen match 88, Parameter expressivity 90, Morphometric validation 88, Source and data traceability 92, Code-to-model traceability 86, Reproducibility package 90. Output judged: docs/media/dactylioceras_commune_turing_wavelength_s0_comparison.png: rendered output of models/2026-delphi10000-dactylioceras-commune-turing-wavelength-s0.py at 8c95fb91d41c76d640c8216d24030d8fd3768487, image/png, 712580 B, 1512×984 px, artifact_sha256 e35739c0fa90e8db7a96fc27ace552f21eb2705ce3a3e02fa08d8c9c253f9720 (sha256 e35739c0fa90e8db7a96fc27ace552f21eb2705ce3a3e02fa08d8c9c253f9720), spec_fingerprint 250d9efaee72b1c988aa7b69152735c73f811d95d1843ab2b2c5433409d97e1d. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: 250d9efaee72b1c988aa7b69152735c73f811d95d1843ab2b2c5433409d97e1d; artifact_sha256: e35739c0fa90e8db7a96fc27ace552f21eb2705ce3a3e02fa08d8c9c253f9720; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/dactylioceras_commune_turing_wavelength_s0/dactylioceras_commune_specimen.jpg=c309b077fb0c3b68..., datasets/dactylioceras_commune_turing_wavelength_s0/dactylioceras_commune_turing_wavelength_s0_reference.json=a8f717691a831459...}. Supersedes audit: 2026-10-27-dactylioceras-commune-turing-wavelength-s0-audit. Claim boundary: reported_in_source: Turing 1952 critical wavenumber and Schnakenberg 1979 kinetics. | Meinhardt and Klingler 1987 and Fowler, Meinhardt and Prusinkiewicz 1992: pigment laid down at a molluscan aperture. | García-Ruiz, Checa and Rivas 1990 and Lutz and Boyajian 1995: ammonoid sutures are morphogenetic and fractal. | James St. John, CC BY 2.0: 57 mm Whitby Formation shell, Toarcian. | Catalogue: 181 Ma, 2.419e-05 m, D_f = 1.55, Ceratites 1.088 mm at 240 Ma, Placenticeras 2.53 mm at 75 Ma.; reconstructed_in_script: Du = 5.789 and Dv = 41.680 µm² per time so the k_c formula returns 24.19 µm at ratio 7.2. | Eigenvector-seeded PDE growth rates versus analytical sigma(k). | Outer-whorl rib harmonic 44 and spacing 3.484 mm from the photograph. | Accretion GIF whose last frame is the specimen, plus a 216 µm stripe patch where 24.19 µm is resolved.; transfer_boundary: Aperture pigment reaction-diffusion is transferred to a 24 µm periostracal patch of an ammonite. The whole-shell pixels are the fossil, not a PDE solution. | Neighbor organ-scale wavelengths are the intervals tiled by this detail wave. Their diffusion coefficients are not reused.; does_not_claim: 24 µm stripes are not resolved across the 57 mm photograph. | D_f = 1.55 was not measured on an exposed suture in this image. | The PDE did not generate the pyrite texture. | No nanopublication was signed: ~/.nanopub/profile.yml is absent. | No second language model scored this audit.." ;
        dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
        pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> ;
        pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
        pk:evidenceAgainst "open need [specimen_comparison/morphometric-validation, pressure P=2.2]: Remeasure suture fractal dimension on an exposed septal trace. Still open; the vendored photo is an exterior.",
            "remediation needed: Residual: D_f = 1.55 is still the catalogue suture dimension. An exposed septal trace would be required to remeasure it on this species.",
            "remediation needed: Residual: nanopub signing was not available (~/.nanopub/profile.yml absent). The audit is unsigned.",
            "remediation needed: Residual: one 57 mm Whitby shell. A second concretion would test whether harmonic 44 is typical." ;
        pk:hasScore "0.895"^^xsd:double ;
        pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> a pk:Model ;
        rdfs:label "Grok 4.7 builder-assessor, loop 3159 pass 2" ;
        dct:identifier "grok-4.7" ;
        prov:actedOnBehalfOf <https://orcid.org/0000-0000-0000-0000> .
}

